prompts.template:
Here is the script for an episode called "{title}".

{role:script}

Where would a listener stop listening? Be specific about timestamps or sections. Name what rambles, what over-explains, and what the episode is avoiding. Do not rewrite it — say what is wrong.

The opening of an episode called "{title}":

{role:script}

Judge only the first thirty seconds as written. Would a new listener keep going? Give three concrete ways to make the open sharper, and say what to cut, not what to add.

The script for "{title}":

{role:script}

The show notes for it:

{role:notes}

What does the episode cover that the notes miss? What do the notes promise that the script never delivers? List the gaps, do not rewrite the notes.

The script for an episode called "{title}":

{role:script}

Pick three moments that would work as a standalone clip under ninety seconds. For each, give the rough boundary and one sentence on why it stands alone. No explanations beyond that.

